# ◈ packages.desktop.list — usable live-environment desktop
#
# Split into its own matrix group (rather than folded into
# packages.graphics.list) because Firefox alone can take hours to compile —
# keeping it isolated means it doesn't extend the graphics group's build
# time, and it gets its own ccache so repeat builds aren't starting cold.
#
# CORRECTED from an earlier revision: added -system-libvpx to firefox's USE
# overrides. Firefox's system-libvpx USE flag pulls in >=media-libs/libvpx-
# 1.8.2[postproc], but the only available libvpx satisfying that is masked
# outright in this tree (not a USE-flag issue autounmask can fix — a real
# package mask). Disabling system-libvpx makes firefox build its own
# bundled libvpx instead, sidestepping the masked package entirely.
#
# ON FIREFOX-BIN: checked — Mozilla's official firefox-bin package is built
# against glibc, not musl. On a pure musl system it won't run without
# gcompat (a glibc compatibility shim), which isn't a good fit here given
# AthanorOS's musl-first minimalism — installing gcompat just to run one
# glibc binary works against the whole point of the profile. So this is a
# genuine from-source build, not a shortcut. Known rough edges building
# Firefox under musl+llvm (both solvable, both already hit by others):
#   - LTO can stack-overflow linking libxul.so, since musl's default stack
#     (80KB) is much smaller than glibc's (2-10MB) — fix is linking with
#     -Wl,-z,stack-size=N or building clang/lld with a larger default stack.
#   - Firefox's build system assumes a glibc rust target by default; needs
#     the musl rust target instead (modern rustc/Gentoo ebuilds generally
#     handle this correctly today, but worth confirming with the actual
#     firefox ebuild revision in your synced tree).
#
# sway itself is a full tiling Wayland compositor (gui-wm/sway — Wayland
# compositors live under gui-wm in Gentoo, not gui-apps; corrected from an
# earlier revision) — as opposed to cage's single-app kiosk mode previously
# in packages.graphics.list. foot is included as a minimal terminal
# (gui-apps/foot — also corrected, it's not under x11-terms), since sway
# needs at least one to be useful standalone.

gui-wm/sway
gui-apps/foot
www-client/firefox            use:-tests,-debug,-system-libvpx
